From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Smith <scott@newtrostudios.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:36:31 -0400
Subject: remotesmith(0702): show the host fingerprint without ID-server
 registration

FLOW-2, AC-43 (whole-product review finding 3). The tray (host facts) and Settings
("fingerprint" over IPC) showed the host key fingerprint only once an ID server had confirmed
the key, so a LAN-only host that never registered had nothing to compare during enrollment.
Both now show the fingerprint of the signing key the host's handshake signs with
(Config::get_key_pair, as server::identity_handshake uses), which is exactly what a controller
pins from the direct route. Test: two fresh, never-registered host keys each show a
fingerprint, they differ, and each equals the pin taken from that host's direct handshake.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
